iv><div class="lg:col-span-8" data-astro-cid-7a6hbtlg><h2 id="demand-forecasting-title" class="h-section" data-astro-cid-7a6hbtlg>Demand forecasting</h2><p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted" data-astro-cid-7a6hbtlg>weekly forecasts, stock levels, staffing plans</p><p class="mt-8 text-xl leading-relaxed" data-astro-cid-7a6hbtlg>Forecasts by product and location with a range around every number, so buyers can see how sure the model is.</p><div class="prose-orrery mt-8" data-astro-cid-7a6hbtlg><p>We forecast whatever drives your costs: units, orders, calls or staff hours. Each forecast comes with a back-test, so you can see how the model would have done last year before you trust it this year.</p>
<h2 id="what-we-model">What we model</h2>
<ul>
<li>Seasonality and holidays, including the ones that move every year</li>
<li>Promotions and price changes, if you have the history</li>
<li>Stock-outs, which hide real demand in your sales data</li>
<li>New products, using the closest existing ones as a guide</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="when-we-say-no">When we say no</h2>
<p>With less than eighteen months of history, a forecasting model rarely beats a well-kept spreadsheet. We tell you that in the first week and bill for the first week only.</p>
